# XSH gethostname()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.gethostname.001
anchor     functions/gethostname.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With a buffer much larger than any host name, gethostname() returns 0, the name is null-terminated, it is no longer than {HOST_NAME_MAX} (when that limit is known), and a second call gives the same name.
note       The limit is taken from sysconf(_SC_HOST_NAME_MAX), or the macro if sysconf reports none.
test       t/001-name-terminated.c

assertion  XSH.gethostname.002
anchor     functions/gethostname.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With namelen one less than the length of the name, gethostname() does not write beyond namelen bytes, and the bytes written are the first namelen bytes of the name (the returned name is truncated, whatever the return value).
note       Whether the result is null-terminated and the return value in this case are not specified. NOTINUSE when the name has fewer than two characters.
test       t/002-truncation.c

assertion  XSH.gethostname.003
anchor     functions/gethostname.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With namelen one more than the length of the name, gethostname() returns 0 and the buffer holds the full name, null-terminated.
test       t/003-exact-fit.c
